+## Building instructions
+
+Every finished build gets LEGO-style instructions on the website. On the Build
+page, a finished build shows "Open building instructions"; the Guide gallery
+links them for past builds too. The page is `/records/<record_id>/instructions`:
+
+- a cover with the finished model, then one page per step, then the parts list;
+- each step shows its number and a parts box (a picture of each part, "2x");
+- the model as built so far, framed so it fills the page; the new parts drop in
+  and glow once, then stay outlined in yellow; a part that is mostly hidden, or a
+  lone small part, is lifted off its spot with a red arrow to it (at most two per
+  step); a step whose parts go on different sides is split, one step per side;
+  a part never shares a step with the part it attaches to (that one comes first);
+  you can drag to turn it and scroll to zoom;
+- the parts list says which of your sets each piece comes from (builds made on
+  the website keep their inventory, with sets, as `inventory.json` in the record);
+- arrow keys or the slider move between steps; "Save as PDF" renders every page
+  and opens the print dialog (choose "Save as PDF"): one step per sheet.
+
+The data comes from the stepped LDraw file only (`out/build.stepped.ldr`, or
+`out/build.ldr` when it has step markers): `build.py` is never run for it.
